      "id": 1,
      "text": "Delhi was first settled in 1865, shortly after the Civil War, and organized as a township in 1876.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delhi%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was platted in 1884 by Alfred M. after the railroad arrived, giving it a strategic rail link.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Delhi_Minnesota",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Delhi Coronet Band Hall, built in 1896, was financed by the local band and featured a distinctive false‑front and belfry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Delhi_Minnesota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The band hall became the venue where Delhi incorporated as a city on November 25, 1902, and held its first elections.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delhi%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The band hall was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1984 for its role in politics and social life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Delhi_Minnesota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
